TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"baseRevision":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","blocked":[{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"blockedBy":["morning-ledger"],"taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"blockedBy":["catalog-handoff"],"taskId":"catalog-handoff"},{"blockedBy":["rdma-package"],"taskId":"rdma-package"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-proxy"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-tp2"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling"],"taskId":"cp-bench"},{"blockedBy":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff"],"taskId":"cp-close"}],"campaign":"flashnext","checkpoints":[],"closingSummary":null,"complete":false,"deferrals":[],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/15","diagnosis":"Aborted in the lane stage before any worktree was prepared, so no worker ever ran and no task content was implicated. The recorded failure is a flow-error whose detail is the harness exception FlowAdmissionDenied (code admission-denied, ordinal 4, at line 3377 column 25) with an empty details object; exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, meaning no command was executed and no gate ran. gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason 'task failed before a worktree was prepared' at base rev all-zeros. Nothing in the task morning-ledger points at the failure: the sole acceptance criterion ledger-sections is a plain grep over docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the authorized docs conflict domain, and it was never evaluated. The dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are also not implicated, because dependency resolution would surface as a task-level block rather than an admission denial raised inside the flow engine itself. Admission denial at lane entry with no stderr, no exit code, and no worktree is a scheduler/session fault in the machinery that admits lanes, not an authorable defect in the repository and not a gate-contract or authority problem the operator must grant. The correct disposition is therefore to charge the bounded machinery-retry budget and re-admit the lane unchanged; if admission is denied again at the same ordinal, the fault is durable in the flow layer and should be escalated to the operator rather than retried further.","taskId":"morning-ledger","verdict":"blocked"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/18","diagnosis":"Failed at lane admission before any worktree, worker invocation, or gate execution occurred, so no task-content defect is implicated. Evidence: the failure stage is `lane` with verdict `flow-error` and detail `FlowAdmissionDenied` / code `admission-denied` (ordinal 4, empty details), exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason \"task failed before a worktree was prepared\". Because the flow controller refused to admit the lane, the worker never read specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5 and never created handoff/catalog-row.patch or handoff/README.md; the sole acceptance criterion catalog-patch-wellformed was never evaluated, and there is no failing check id or offending path to cite. Nothing in the task is at fault: it is an implementation task with no dependencies, a single conflict domain of \"handoff\" that is also its only authorized write prefix, and no needs-authority envelope was returned. There is likewise no out-of-task cause to name — no missing authority, no gate-contract defect, no upstream source fix, since the denial carries no adjudicable reason payload and no work product exists to attribute it to. This is a scheduler/session-level admission fault in the campaign machinery (for example lane-slot or conflict-domain admission contention on \"handoff\"), which is precisely what the bounded machinery-retry budget covers; a re-admission of the identical lane at revision sha256:3a04f0fc89c3e88303af3a5b38fc8a4bd52f2f81715bfecfc42bdc04ba5c2269 is the correct next action. If admission is denied again with the same code and still-empty details, the recurrence stops being incidental and should be escalated to the operator as a flow-configuration problem rather than continuing to consume retries.","taskId":"catalog-handoff","verdict":"blocked"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/21","diagnosis":"Failed during lane admission before any worktree, worker, or gate execution occurred, so nothing about the task's content was exercised. The failure record carries stage \"lane\", verdict \"flow-error\", a null exit code, empty stderr, and detail {\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}} with no populated details payload. Corroborating evidence: gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes is empty, and the diff block reports available=false with reason \"task failed before a worktree was prepared\" and a null head against the all-zero base revision. There is therefore no failing check id and no offending path to cite, because no acceptance criterion ran; the sole criterion rdma-package-sound was never invoked. The task definition itself shows no admission-blocking defect: it declares no dependencies, its conflictDomains [\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"] cover every path its goal directs it to write (host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh, host/rdma/attended-bringup.md, host/rdma/ab-protocol.md, and the tests suite extension), and its read-only references to specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6, specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md, specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-hardening-addendum.md, and scripts/stage-weights.sh require no write authority outside those domains. The worker envelope did not request authority, so the always-blocked needs-authority path does not apply. That leaves an orchestration-side admission refusal — the flow machinery declining to open the lane at ordinal 4 — rather than an actionable in-task fix or an out-of-task authority, dependency, or gate-contract defect. Re-dispatch of the identical task revision sha256:b322b54d6da9831c25a2e55569a9a8ce4c293840285b6225b2760d2c20ee9460 against a healthy lane is the correct next action; it should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget and not the task's two-attempt cap. If admission is denied again with the same code and an empty details payload, escalate to the operator as a flow-layer fault rather than re-diagnosing the task, since no repository change under host/rdma or tests could alter this outcome.","taskId":"rdma-package","verdict":"blocked"}],"escalation":null,"frontier":[{"argv":["bash","scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"],"dependencies":[],"id":"cp-weights","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:991f181013631a76e48098eddf0692acf3c0f4ce661a1ad1b82cd6fcbef45237","runtimeMaxSec":10800,"title":"Checkpoint: stage the workload checkpoint onto both nodes"}],"inputEpochs":{"bench-harness":"sha256:2352e45654aa40b953261c40e9f6ec94f1092cad33d430f9ecf48e6f10e3c5eb","catalog-handoff":"sha256:94d761662378a9c6a78bb5f60b9cd6cfbc89e56419945e15d63b493ed994f4e9","container-recipe":"sha256:597bcbb9ee96cc98997c446dcd92c490489300e35163a5d59b7037f6030d6758","cp-bench":"sha256:b664febb5bb3a52e84267bd7c4f343753c56be5d98796fc517cc6a565847b003","cp-build":"sha256:2a39e30082d563c7b5088199b5da6df98513e32d371d384e9c33f8d8f5a6a629","cp-close":"sha256:d0561387144934af0071a18388de11968a5dd96ba199ce6599b35b46905fa14e","cp-proxy":"sha256:a3d50f72301ae0c33b0b2aa0e8b8533dc139372f2f06ccfefd10b33dc9fbf05c","cp-smoke":"sha256:5678368f6a54d9797cbd69e04644d2f3d542b92653c8fc00d1b0881d4cb76ecb","cp-tp2":"sha256:6bb34cc2a74aca9267004f096723ac202a9715290bbf3b51c05b9e55aa5c91e9","cp-weights":"sha256:7e1479062d9c8f01724cea119dd68290d90e6501b7c3b6d232f254f082013990","host-tooling":"sha256:b771d06ffbc5cd093ade0388dbf7dd8d390243cf5e3a7e92dce2bedb4b78a0ff","instruments":"sha256:347517ad56e50308317a8a6db7e931c56d2b850afeec55dbaa2f514bb01b333c","morning-ledger":"sha256:5299ae20113a6c75b529f2e56d080294e9b3ee2931ba72466d381b49dafa1747","proxy-tooling":"sha256:a2af59b8d6e320b5a080b8deb94c795832cec0afe9188bdf13e51e29809b6793","rdma-package":"sha256:7362f764d07dfb573ee2a7f3bece7b6b4fa5d7173e0e6b23d0f7f5b9ed9d8e2a"},"merged":[{"mergeCommit":"c1363cb2308e16f3d96bd92e8cde7c94261d4cb9","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/container-recipe-6e8621b55de3a3a9","revision":"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","taskId":"container-recipe"},{"mergeCommit":"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f","revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"}],"outcomes":[],"quiescent":false,"remaining":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package","cp-weights","cp-build","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close"],"repository":"mecattaf/flashnext","retries":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/23","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/24","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/13","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/14","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"morning-ledger"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/16","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"catalog-handoff"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/17","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"catalog-handoff"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/19","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"rdma-package"},{"attempt":2,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/20","reason":"Stage `lane` faulted.\n\n{\"name\":\"FlowAdmissionDenied\",\"code\":\"admission-denied\",\"line\":3377,\"column\":25,\"ordinal\":4,\"details\":{}}","taskId":"rdma-package"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/22","reason":"Stage `checkpoint:record` faulted.\n\n{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a04d21-e32f-7d33-bc95-c7c2eec557ff\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false}}}}","taskId":"cp-weights"}],"schemaVersion":1,"source":{"path":"silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json","revision":"a82f09edbb73626db818cc2d8dd288455955787e","sha256":"sha256:a38d2fe61602b34c1d81bd3afbd3edf33c9e705952d6f5d0e0f726f910a4c3a0"},"tasks":[{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n container/build.sh && grep -q 'torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'mecattaf/vllm' container/Containerfile && grep -q 'flashnext:dev' container/build.sh && grep -qi 'MIT' container/Containerfile"],"description":"The recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.","id":"recipe-pins"}],"conflictDomains":["container","results/receipts"],"deliveredBehaviors":["A reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set","A build receipt the receipts gate can grade"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\"build\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.","id":"container-recipe","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3","IMPORTS.md","specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},"revision":"sha256:6e8621b55de3a3a9c646edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","title":"Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v"],"description":"All three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.","id":"instruments-compile-with-notices"}],"conflictDomains":["container/rootfs","tests"],"deliveredBehaviors":["Instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill-switches, default off","Notice headers travel with every adapted module"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the FN_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a FN_PROFILE window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env FN_EXPERT_UNION with FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT). Every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. Add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). Boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.","id":"instruments","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md","specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/receipts-verify.py"]},"revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","title":"Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","for f in host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh; do bash -n \"$f\"; done && grep -q 'PYTHONHASHSEED=0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'thunderbolt0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'ExecStopPost' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && ! grep -q 'WantedBy' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v"],"description":"Env doctrine present, units teardown-safe, all scripts syntax-clean, host tests pass.","id":"host-doctrine"}],"conflictDomains":["host","scripts/run-tp2.sh","tests"],"deliveredBehaviors":["One command stands the pair service; one command tears it down; failure cannot strand ranks","First light produces the four receipts the ladder grades"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Write the host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh per spec claims 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 6.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, #r6), composing the disciplines in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 5 and specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 5. host/fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0; PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85; HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1; inductor and triton cache dirs under the state directory, never tmpfs; NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME set ONLY to the Thunderbolt rails that carry a routable /30 IP (rail 0 thunderbolt0/10.99.0.x is guaranteed; rail 1 thunderbolt1 is trained-but-IP-unconfigured today per dotfiles modules/lowlat-cluster.nix and MUST NOT be listed until it has a peer IP — a peerless link-local rail in the list hangs RCCL bootstrap; the env file computes this from `ip -br addr` at write time and logs which rails it chose, rather than hardcoding both); NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY (an ibverbs device now exists on the rails from the pre-arm bake; without this pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides unproven RDMA — sockets are the transport of record until the attended morning A/B, evidence host/rdma/ab-protocol.md); VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_; VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; a loud comment forbidding exports of engine defaults read through is-set probes. host/fn-cluster-up.sh: podman on both nodes (worker over ssh on the wire), distributed head on the coordinator and worker join, worker python pool capped small, a hard two-GPU gate before serve, then the serve process at tensor-parallel size 2 with eager execution, model directory /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8, served name flashnext; reap stranded serve processes before start and gate on zero residue. host/fn-cluster-down.sh: idempotent teardown both nodes. host/fn-preflight.sh: byte-diff of both ranks' FN_ env, latency-hold device read on both ends, per-rail link-speed record, round-trip probe on both rails. host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service: oneshot, RemainAfterExit, ExecStopPost teardown, no install section. scripts/run-tp2.sh: preflight, up, two greedy 300-token completions byte-compared, residency read after 50 warmed decode tokens (GTT per rank from sysfs plus process RSS plus table page-cache residency), fidelity capture (fixed-prompt losses and frontier logits under results/), then a 262144-context probe, writing receipts tp2.json, residency.json, fidelity.json, context.json per the receipts-verify.py schema. Extend tests/test_repo_invariants.py-adjacent coverage with tests/test_host_tooling.py asserting the env file carries the doctrine lines and unit files carry ExecStopPost and no WantedBy install. Boundaries: touch only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, and tests/.","id":"host-tooling","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4","specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6","specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md","specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/stage-weights.sh","scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},"revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","title":"Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -m py_compile bench/fn-stream-client.py && bash -n bench/run-matrix.sh && python3 -m unittest tests.test_bench_client -v"],"description":"Client compiles, separation test passes, matrix script is syntax-clean.","id":"bench-honest-client"}],"conflictDomains":["bench","tests"],"deliveredBehaviors":["A client whose prefill number is a measurement, not a proxy","A matrix whose every number carries its protocol"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Write bench/fn-stream-client.py and bench/run-matrix.sh per spec claims 6.2 and 6.3 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6). The client measures per-request time-to-first-token client-side AND scrapes the server metrics endpoint to separate scheduler queue wait from prompt processing — the reference harness's client published a prefill column that duplicated its first-token column (specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md section 4.4); ours must not. Emit CSV with explicit column semantics in a header comment, plus a sha256 fingerprint of every completion's token ids. run-matrix.sh: arms interleaved A-B-B-A, three loads per arm, medians reported, depth series 0, 10240, 102400 tokens, speculative decoding on and off arms, results committed under results/ and a bench.json receipt {loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}. Add tests/test_bench_client.py: feed the client parser a fixture with known queue and processing times and assert the two columns separate them. Boundaries: touch only bench/ and tests/.","id":"bench-harness","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6","specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/receipts-verify.py"]},"revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","title":"Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.","id":"proxy-scripts-clean"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.","id":"proxy-serve-flags"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh"],"description":"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.","id":"proxy-checkpoint-layout"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","[ -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]"],"description":"The lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task's commit.","id":"proxy-lane-clean"}],"conflictDomains":["scripts/make-proxy.sh","scripts/run-proxy.sh","tests","results/receipts/proxy.json"],"deliveredBehaviors":["The admitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded"],"dependencies":["container-recipe"],"goal":"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.","id":"proxy-tooling","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4","specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md","specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},"revision":"sha256:ee1de7acf13cebd8c4da8186aaea8b7a99f092ba537fd379c111c5f42e955c17","title":"Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'Receipt review' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Open items' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Promotion checklist' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Optimization menu' docs/MORNING.md && grep -qi 'blocker' docs/MORNING.md && test -s docs/ANNOUNCE.md"],"description":"The ledger carries its five sections and the announcement draft exists.","id":"ledger-sections"}],"conflictDomains":["docs"],"deliveredBehaviors":["The operator's first ten minutes are a checklist, not archaeology","The community post is ready to publish with the benchmark numbers"],"dependencies":["host-tooling","bench-harness"],"goal":"Write docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 6.4 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6): a receipt review table (one row per receipt under results/receipts with status and the bound it was graded against), the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state), the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13), the optimization menu (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md), and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/.","id":"morning-ledger","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6","specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7","IMPORTS.md"],"styleReferences":["README.md"]},"revision":"sha256:4c0b640cab49ea7ac3b57b4e23f66c726b92fcce08e77d0f8816814181c3ba0a","title":"Render the morning ledger and the announcement draft"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","git apply --stat handoff/catalog-row.patch >/dev/null && test -s handoff/README.md"],"description":"The patch parses as a git patch and the handoff note exists.","id":"catalog-patch-wellformed"}],"conflictDomains":["handoff"],"deliveredBehaviors":["The morning catalog declaration is one git apply plus one review, not authoring work"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Write handoff/catalog-row.patch per spec claim 5.2 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5): a git format patch against the fleet configuration repository adding the workload checkpoint as a snapshot-layout artifact row assigned to both hosts, following the existing snapshot-layout precedent row in that repository's model library file, with pinned upstream revision and per-file byte counts read from the staged copy under /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8 (or from the library mount when staging has not finished). Add handoff/README.md explaining exactly what the operator applies and verifies in the morning. The patch is prepared, never applied, by this campaign. Boundaries: touch only handoff/.","id":"catalog-handoff","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5","specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md"],"styleReferences":["THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"]},"revision":"sha256:3a04f0fc89c3e88303af3a5b38fc8a4bd52f2f81715bfecfc42bdc04ba5c2269","title":"Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator"},{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '503c5ae1e72aa9ed91925dafa3d82ee2e992747f' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '76ba39b630a70accb72f19388eefe48844b50eb8' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && ! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*(sudo[[:space:]]+)?(insmod|modprobe)[[:space:]]' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -qi 'physically present' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'worker first' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'deploy' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && test -s host/rdma/ab-protocol.md"],"description":"Scripts syntax-clean, pins present, no auto-install, attended language present.","id":"rdma-package-sound"}],"conflictDomains":["host/rdma","tests"],"deliveredBehaviors":["Tomorrow's attended RDMA bring-up is one script plus one checklist plus one adoption gate","No unsigned module can load unattended from anything this repo ships"],"dependencies":[],"goal":"The bootstrap session scoped an operator-attended RDMA bring-up package (spec ruling P7, claim 6.4 — specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6): host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh (pinned out-of-tree module fetch, kernel-version and secure-boot guards, staged install only), host/rdma/attended-bringup.md (the coordinated-reboot checklist with the port-controller recovery path), host/rdma/ab-protocol.md (the socket-versus-verbs adoption gate). If those files already exist in the tree, verify them against the reference bring-up doctrine in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 7 plus specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-hardening-addendum.md and fix defects; if absent, author them from those sections' pins. Hard rules: nothing GPL is vendored — the two out-of-tree repositories are fetched at their pinned commits by the script; nothing installs or loads automatically; one rail only; the checklist states plainly that bring-up happens with the operator physically present, starts only after a committed socket-transport benchmark exists under results/, opens with the worker deploy-path repoint off the fast rail, and orders reboots worker first, never both at once. Extend the tests suite so the syntax sweep covers host/rdma and a test asserts the two pin commits appear in fetch-and-build.sh. Boundaries: touch only host/rdma and tests/.","id":"rdma-package","kind":"implementation","readFirst":{"specSections":["specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6","specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md"],"styleReferences":["scripts/stage-weights.sh"]},"revision":"sha256:b322b54d6da9831c25a2e55569a9a8ce4c293840285b6225b2760d2c20ee9460","title":"Integrate the operator-attended RDMA package under host/rdma"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"],"dependencies":[],"id":"cp-weights","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:991f181013631a76e48098eddf0692acf3c0f4ce661a1ad1b82cd6fcbef45237","runtimeMaxSec":10800,"title":"Checkpoint: stage the workload checkpoint onto both nodes"},{"argv":["bash","container/build.sh"],"dependencies":["container-recipe","instruments"],"id":"cp-build","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:03219517866e525ca2f438c3896635f19315405ab7ff351108bab2f67b8c46c2","runtimeMaxSec":14400,"title":"Checkpoint: the container engine build"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"dependencies":["cp-build"],"id":"cp-smoke","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:f6d3bc428003f8bb40eb0422b1c3199fd1957b0cf966ff153c17a9b5d5bc4225","runtimeMaxSec":1800,"title":"Checkpoint: in-container smoke — identity, fp8 cast, admission"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"dependencies":["cp-smoke","proxy-tooling"],"id":"cp-proxy","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:6fbf0ea685ac3069755fa819434b3eee4c2f32dd4214e7d218b7f20c5659a0a6","runtimeMaxSec":3600,"title":"Checkpoint: proxy checkpoint first light, single node"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/run-tp2.sh"],"dependencies":["cp-proxy","cp-weights","host-tooling"],"id":"cp-tp2","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:d196a72e37ff2e8a46157397702992e95af39dbda52bf246dc953d8ffc1bdbb8","runtimeMaxSec":10800,"title":"Checkpoint: pair first light, residency, fidelity, full context"},{"argv":["bash","bench/run-matrix.sh"],"dependencies":["cp-tp2","bench-harness"],"id":"cp-bench","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:27c5836591232ed454a208322c2edf3d2ef5bfd48b2229cfc7eb8d9347d152eb","runtimeMaxSec":14400,"title":"Checkpoint: the counterbalanced bench matrix"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -m unittest discover -s tests && python3 scripts/receipts-verify.py && FN_FORK_STRICT=1 bash scripts/verify-fork.sh"],"dependencies":["cp-bench","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff"],"id":"cp-close","kind":"checkpoint","revision":"sha256:b7c99445b074b20ed636442dd80d830240465c7437ae93f9c75c14b793aa8546","runtimeMaxSec":3600,"title":"Checkpoint: full verification pass over everything the night produced"}],"warnings":["task proxy-tooling latched for human attention after 10 lifetime attempt receipts (hard limit 10)"]}
